1 OCCU Väpnare (Riddare) och Herre i Hov, Kjent som "gamle Karl i Hov"., Ridder og jordeier, squire, Væpner og jordeier, Væpner (ridder) og jordeier., Carolus Petri kallad, Ridder og Jordeier, Ridder, Väpnare och ägare av sätesgården Hov
2 CONC  i Hackås
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carl Pedersen (Karl Persson or Pettersson) of Hof has been considered the earliest verified ancestor of the noble family of Skanke (Schanke, Schancke, Schanche, etc), and its Hackås line, based on interpretations o
2 CONC f contemporary literature. He lived in about 1360-1430. His son Ørjan Karlsson Skanke was a knight and a captain  in about 1450s in Jämtland-Härjedalen, which was a Norwegian province since 1178, conquered by Sweden in 1645. The f
2 CONC amily has branches in Norway, Sweden and Denmark. One branch of the family was ennobled in Sweden in the 1600s as Skunck, but that branch is extinct.. Earlier roots are at issue, as well as the origin of the noble family of Blix, 
2 CONC which is married into the Skanke family in several branches. A theory of less certainty, suggested especially by the Genealogist George Vaughan Chichester Young in 1986, is that the Skancke family originiates from the last kings o
2 CONC f Isle of Man, and from Charles the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT The earliest DNA verified ancestor of the Skancke family and its Hackås line, the older Hov branch, is https://www.geni.com/people/Peder-Jensson-Skanke/6000000007828172937 (born 1577 in Hov, Hackås), traditionally considered a gre
2 CONC at great great great grandson of Carl Pedersen along a strict male line.Descendants to several of his sons share the same haplogroup. A biological relationship between Carl and Peder has neither been supported nor disproved, by DN
2 CONC A tests as of April 2021, but DNA tests show that several of the branches of the Schanke family do not have an agnatic biological relation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
