1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.gurihus.net/slekt/tng/getperson.php?personID=I2641&tree=DG
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Stilling : Gårdbruker, postmann.
2 CONT
2 CONT I 1642 eide Håver halve Torgunsbøen (1/2 hud), dessuten 2 skinn i Bren den under Presterud. Begge deler var odelsgods. I 1644 eide "Håver Går der og medarvinger "
2 CONT
2 CONT det ovennevnte samt de 4 skinn som faren hadde eid i Nordeng i 1642. E n av disse medarvingene var broren Jon Johannessen Rud, jfr.formynders kap ved skifte på Gårder 12.juni 1693, og det var sannsynligvis en søs ter, gift med Amu
2 CONC nd Taraldsen Lien. I 1670 lot Christen Gundersen Torg unsbøen i Torpa tinglyse et "løsenbrev" fra sin "frende" Håver Johanne ssen Gårder på halvparten i Torgunsbøen, datert Gårder 5 april 1669. ( Christen født ca. 1612).
2 CONT
2 CONT Den halve huden  i Torgunsbøen ble forøvrig eid av Peder og Torgrim Kn udssønner Finden i 1624, med 3 skinn hver. (VSLT nr. 2/96 s.107ff.) Si den ikke Håvers far kan sees å ha eid noe i Torgunsbøen kan denne odel en vel stamme fra
2 CONC  Håvers ukjente mor?
2 CONT
2 CONT Håver satt på Gårder i 1642, 1647 og 1666. Gården var krongods. Isegri m var egen gård i 1647 og utover, men er i moderne tid en del av Gårde r. Gården var "bondegods" i 1647. Det står ikke hvem som eide den,me n brukeren var Gutt
2 CONC orm. Det er ikke usannsynlig at Håver eide Isegri m i 1647. Den 12-6-1693 var det skifte på Gårder etter Håvers (2.) kon e Kirsten Eriksdtr. og der nevnes Håvers gods:
2 CONT
2 CONT Odelsgods 1 hud i Isegrim
2 CONT
2 CONT Kjøpegods  2 skinn i Markestad, som brukes under Isegrim.
2 CONT
2 CONT I skiftet ble også nevnt barna Johannes Åsen (Landåsen) og Torsten Hår stad fra første ekteskap. Fra et skifte i 1718 vet vi at han også hadd e Hans Lunde fra dette ekteskapet. Johannes og Torsten ble oppgitt å v ære hhv. 22 og 14
2 CONC  år i 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra VSLT nr. 4/94 side 276ff. og nr. 3/95 side 211: Tingboka for Toten ,Vardal og Biri 10. mars og 18 juni 1666 angående tilsynsmennene for G jevle-godset-arven etter sorenskriver Hans Pedersen Gjevle:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tilsynsmennene var Håver Johannessen Gårder og Elling Reiersen Øvre Sk iaker.(Elling var sønn av Reier Olufsen Øvre Skiaker som igjen var søn n av Oluf Lodinsen Landåsen.) 3 av vitnene ble avvist fordi de var i f or nær slekt med 
2 CONC tilsynsmennene:
2 CONT
2 CONT Torsten Halvorsen Rud i Biri var "besvogret"med Håver Gårder og Ellin g Reiersen Øvre Skiaker. (I 1697 får vi vite at Torstens kone het Helg a Endresdtr. Hun var antagelig datter av Endre Endresen Brone i Nordsi nni og hans 2. kon
2 CONC e Damøy Augustinusdtr. Død før 1670. Endre hadde ogs å barn fra første ekteskap.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Eriksen Nes var "i slektskap" med både Håver Gårder og Elling Ski aker. Erik var sønn av Erik Endresen Brone og halvbror av Helga Endres dtr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Torsten Engebretsen Setton (født ca 1609) var "besvogret" med Håver Gå rder. Torsten var gift med Guri Gulbrandsdtr. fra Esbjug. Noen konkre t forbindelse kan her ikke bevises. (VSLT nr. 1/92 s. 58ff viser at To rsten Engebretsen 
2 CONC var gift 1. gang med en enke etter Oluf Eriksen Sett on. Denne Oluf Setton eide i odelsskattelisten 1624 bl.a. 1 hud og 2 s kinn i ISEGRIM ! Den resterende part, 9 skinn tilhørte LychAskvig, kan skje gift med en datter av Erik Set
2 CONC ton. Erik O. Setton eide i 1615 hel e Isegrim på 2 huder. Det kan etter dette synes som om Håver har fåt t Isegrim med sin 2. kone, og at hun kanskje var datter av Erik Settto n?).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Postbonde
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Occupation: Farmer, postman.
2 CONT In 1642, Håver owned half of Torgunsbøen (1/2 hide), also 2 hides in Bren den under Presterud. Both parts were noble estates. In 1644, "Håver Går der og co-heirs" owned the above as well as the 4 skins that the father had owned in
2 CONC  Nordeng in 1642. One of these co-heirs was his brother Jon Johannessen Rud, cf. guardian's cap at transfer of Gårder 12 June 1693, and there was probably a sister, married to Amund Taraldsen Lien. In 1670, Christen Gundersen Torg
2 CONC  unsbøen in Torpa registered a "deed of ransom" from his "cousin" Håver Johanne ssen Gårder on half of Torgunsbøen, dated Gårder 5 April 1669. (Christen born ca. 1612).
2 CONT The half hide in Torgunsbøen was incidentally owned by Peder and Torgrim Kn udssønner Finden in 1624, with 3 hides each. (VSLT no. 2/96 p.107ff.) If it is not possible that Håver's father can be seen to have owned something in Tor
2 CONC gunsbøen, could this odel be descended from Håver's unknown mother?
2 CONT Håver sat on farms in 1642, 1647 and 1666. The farm was crown property. Isegri m was its own farm in 1647 onwards, but is in modern times part of Gårde r. The farm was a "farm estate" in 1647. It is not stated who owned it, but th
2 CONC e user was Guttorm. It is not improbable that Håver owned Isegri in 1647. On 12-6-1693 there was a change in Gårder after Håver's (2nd) wife Kirsten Eriksdtr. and Håver's estate is mentioned there:
2 CONT Odelsgods 1 hud i Isegrim
2 CONT Purchase goods 2 skins in Markestad, which are used under Isegrim.
2 CONT The shift also mentioned the children Johannes Åsen (Landåsen) and Torsten Hår stad from the first marriage. From a transfer in 1718, we know that he also had Hans Lunde from this marriage. Johannes and Torsten were stated to be r
2 CONC espectively. 22 and 14 years in 1666.
2 CONT From VSLT No. 4/94 page 276ff. and no. 3/95 page 211: The court register for Toten, Vardal and Biri 10 March and 18 June 1666 regarding the overseers of the Gjevle estate inheritance by magistrate Hans Pedersen Gjevle:
2 CONT The overseers were Håver Johannessen Gårder and Elling Reiersen Øvre Skiaker. (Elling was the son of Reier Olufsen Øvre Skiaker who in turn was the son of Oluf Lodinsen Landåsen.) 3 of the witnesses were rejected because they were
2 CONC  closely related to the overseers:
2 CONT Torsten Halvorsen Rud in Biri was "brother-in-law" with Håver Gårder and Elling Reiersen Øvre Skiaker. (In 1697 we learn that Torsten's wife's name was Helg a Endresdtr. She was presumably the daughter of Endre Endresen Brone in N
2 CONC ordsi nni and his 2nd wife Damøy Augustinusdtr. Died before 1670. Endre also had children from his first marriage.)
2 CONT Erik Eriksen Nes was "related" to both Håver Gårder and Elling Ski aker. Erik was the son of Erik Endresen Brone and half-brother of Helga Endres dtr.
2 CONT Torsten Engebretsen Setton (born ca. 1609) was "brother-in-law" to Håver Gå rder. Torsten was married to Guri Gulbrandsdtr. from Esbjug. No concrete connection can be proven here. (VSLT no. 1/92 p. 58ff shows that To rsten Engebre
2 CONC tsen was married the first time to a widow of Oluf Eriksen Sett on. This Oluf Setton owned in the estate tax list 1624, among other things, 1 skin and 2 cheeks in ISEGRIM! The remaining part, 9 hides belonged to LychAskvig, may be
2 CONC  married to a daughter of Erik Setton. In 1615 Erik O. Setton owned the whole of Isegrim on 2 hides. It may seem from this that Håver got t Isegrim with his 2nd wife, and that she was perhaps the daughter of Erik Settto n?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Farmer, postman.
2 CONT In 1642, Håver owned half of Torgunsbøen (1/2 hide), also 2 hides in Bren den under Presterud. Both parts were noble estates. In 1644, "Håver Går der og co-heirs" owned the above as well as the 4 skins that the father had owned in
2 CONC  Nordeng in 1642. One of these co-heirs was his brother Jon Johannessen Rud, cf. guardian's cap at transfer of Gårder 12 June 1693, and there was probably a sister, married to Amund Taraldsen Lien. In 1670, Christen Gundersen Torg
2 CONC  unsbøen in Torpa registered a "deed of ransom" from his "cousin" Håver Johanne ssen Gårder on half of Torgunsbøen, dated Gårder 5 April 1669. (Christen born ca. 1612).
2 CONT The half hide in Torgunsbøen was incidentally owned by Peder and Torgrim Kn udssønner Finden in 1624, with 3 hides each. (VSLT no. 2/96 p.107ff.) If it is not possible that Håver's father can be seen to have owned something in Tor
2 CONC gunsbøen, could this odel be descended from Håver's unknown mother?
2 CONT Håver sat on farms in 1642, 1647 and 1666. The farm was crown property. Isegri m was its own farm in 1647 onwards, but is in modern times part of Gårde r. The farm was a "farm estate" in 1647. It is not stated who owned it, but th
2 CONC e user was Guttorm. It is not improbable that Håver owned Isegri in 1647. On 12-6-1693 there was a change in Gårder after Håver's (2nd) wife Kirsten Eriksdtr. and Håver's estate is mentioned there:
2 CONT Odelsgods 1 hud i Isegrim
2 CONT Purchase goods 2 skins in Markestad, which are used under Isegrim.
