2 CONT * Daughter of Lendmann Guttorm Åsulvsen Rein and Eldrid Jonsdatter Smør av Blindheim 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married : '''Guttorm  Ostmansson,''' f. eft. ca. 1130, Sverige, d. mellan 1176 and 1178.  Guttorm Östmanssons sonnesons sonneson. Guttorm Östmansson påstås videre at være datters sonnesons sonneson af hovdingen Östman Gudfastsso
2 CONC n, nævnt på runestenen på Frösön. Guttorm Östmansson var gift med Ingrid Guttormsdtr., datter af Guttorm Åsulfsson til Rein og Eldrid Jonsdtr. Guttorm Åsulfssons mor var Tora Skoftesdtr, som var Ragnhild Erlingsdtr.'s sonnesons da
2 CONC tter. Ragnhild var datter af en sonneson til kong Harald Hårfager.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Guttorm Guttormsson''' f.ca 1160 Svealand d. 1240 Jämtland
2 CONT * '''Helena Guttormsdatter,'''Född: cirka 1167. Död: efter 1210 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#AsulfSkulessonMThoraSkoptisd Project MedLands, Norway Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GUTTORM Asulfsson of Rein, son of ASULF Skulesson & his wife Thora Skoptisdotter'''  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as the son of "Asolf of Reine" & his wife[239].  Morkinskinna names “Ásólfr, the father of Guthormr at Rein” a
2 CONC s the son of “Skúli, the son of Jarl Tostig Godwinson”[240]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: firstly '''ELDRED Jonsdotter'''
2 CONT * Married: secondly '''BERGLJOT,''' daughter of ---. 
2 CONT * Married: thirdly '''SIGRID Thorkilsdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guttorm & his wife had five children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''RANGRID Guttormsdotter .  m firstly BJORN Byrdasven .  m secondly FREDERIK Kjona (-1164).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rangrid & her first husband BJORN had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''ELRID Bjornsdotter.'''  m firstly THORER Skindfeld .  m secondly MAGNUS Erlingsson King of Norway, son of ERLING Ormsen "Skakke/the Sharp" Jarl in Norway & his wife Kristin Sigurdsdotter of Norway (1156-killed 
2 CONC in battle near Fimreite on Sognefjord 15 Jun 1184, bur Bergen, Christ's Church).
2 CONT * 2.         '''INGERID married GUTTORM Ostmansson'''
2 CONT * 3.         '''GUDRUD'''
2 CONT * 4.         '''ASULF Guttormsson'''
2 CONT * 5.         '''BAARD Guttormsson of Rein''' (-1194).  Snorre names Bard as son of "Guthorm of Reine"[241].  Morkinskinna names “Guthormr at Rein” as father of “Bárdr, the father of King Ingi and Skúli jarl”[242].  m firstly ULFHI
2 CONC LD Palsdatter .  m secondly (after 15 Jun 1184) as her second husband, CECILIA Sigurdsdotter, divorced wife of FOLKVID Lagmand in Värmland, illegitimate daughter of SIGURD Haraldsson "Mund" Joint King of Norway & his mistress --- 
2 CONC (-1185).  The Saga of King Sverre records that King Sverre arranged the marriage of "his sister Cecilia" to "Bard Guthormsson of Rein"[243], dated from the context to just after the death of King Magnus [15 Jun 1184].  m thirdly R
2 CONC AGNDID Erlingsdotter .  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baard & his second wife CECILIA Sigurdsdotter had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''INGE Baardsson'''
