1 OCCU Prest i Selbu og Härjedalen, begge Norge
1 TITL Prost
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peder Mathisen (Madsen). Peder Madsen lived in the era of the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Northern Seven Years War (1563-70). The Swedes had invaded Trøndelag but 
2 CONT
2 CONT withdrew when the Treaty of Stettin was signed, ravaging the countryside as they went.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1564, Herr Peder Mattson, priest in Herjedalen, had requested the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dano-Norwegian Crown to grant him a new parish since the Swedes had burnt his down the year before. This is probably the same Peder Mathisen and the Crown granted him the Selbu parish. But he seems to have been a marked man for th
2 CONC e Swedes followed him!
2 CONT
2 CONT "Herr Peder was the priest in Selbu in 1570, when Claus Flemming and a 
2 CONT
2 CONT large troop of soldiers came through Selbu after a raid on Trondheim. According 
2 CONT
2 CONT to tradition, the churchgoers barely escaped the surprise attack, also the 
2 CONT
2 CONT priest. One of his successors, Lauritz, tells that Herr Peder fled on horseback 
2 CONT
2 CONT to Sveg in Herjedalen. He was able to get his son (Mogens) with him but 
2 CONT
2 CONT nothing is known of the rest of his family. It is not unlikely that he had to 
2 CONT
2 CONT leave them and his property and gold to the Swedes' ravaging. Herr Peder never returned to Selbu. He lived in Sveg a long time after. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Peder Mathisen (Madsen). Peder Madsen lived in the era of the
2 CONT
2 CONT Northern Seven Years War (1563-70). The Swedes had invaded Trøndelag but
2 CONT
2 CONT withdrew when the Treaty of Stettin was signed, ravaging the countryside as they went.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1564, Herr Peder Mattson, priest in Herjedalen, had requested the
2 CONT
2 CONT Dano-Norwegian Crown to grant him a new parish since the Swedes had burnt his down the year before. This is probably the same Peder Mathisen and the Crown granted him the Selbu parish. But he seems to have been a marked man for th
2 CONC e Swedes followed him!
2 CONT
2 CONT "Herr Peder was the priest in Selbu in 1570, when Claus Flemming and a
2 CONT
2 CONT large troop of soldiers came through Selbu after a raid on Trondheim. According
2 CONT
2 CONT to tradition, the churchgoers barely escaped the surprise attack, also the
2 CONT
2 CONT priest. One of his successors, Lauritz, tells that Herr Peder fled on horseback
2 CONT
2 CONT to Sveg in Herjedalen. He was able to get his son (Mogens) with him but
2 CONT
2 CONT nothing is known of the rest of his family. It is not unlikely that he had to
2 CONT
2 CONT leave them and his property and gold to the Swedes' ravaging. Herr Peder never returned to Selbu. He lived in Sveg a long time after.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
