1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Skarsholm slægten''' (ca 1205 - ca 1433), '''efterkommere af kong Valdemar Sejr''' Skarsholm slægtens vaaben Våbenskjold: Tværdelt i blåt og sølv, i 1' felt en gående guld leopard el løve, i 2' felt røde hjerter
2 CONC .  På hjelmen leoparden/løven.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Skarsholm slægten stammer fra kong Valdemars Sejrs barn Knud''' (ca 1205 - 1260) med Esbern Snares enke, og den levede i 6 generationer (ca 1205-1432/34).
2 CONT
2 CONT De kaldes Skarsholm slægten efter''' borgen ved Skarresø nær Jyderup''', 15 km ø for Kalundborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Valdemarsson av Skarsholm (ca 1208 - Oct 15, 1260)
2 CONT
2 CONT == Basics ==
2 CONT * Father: Valdemar Sejr, konge av Danmark
2 CONT * Mother: Helena Guttormsdatter, frille (concubine)
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I3058&tree=2
2 CONT * [http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knut_Valdemarsson_av_Danmark Svensk Wikipedia]
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canute,_Duke_of_Reval Engelsk Wikipedia]
2 CONT *[http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Skarsholms%C3%A4tten Adelsvapen] In Swedish
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DENMARK.htm#KnudValdemarsendied1260B MEDLands 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blev 1216 Hertug af Laaland, 1219 Hertug af Estland, blev 1222-23 belejret i Lyndanise af Esterne, 1227 fordrevet fra Estland, 1232 Hertug af Bleking, deltog 1246 i Oprøret mod Kong Erik Plovpenning, blev 1247 sat i Fængsel paa St
2 CONC egehus, men blev Aaret efter befriet af Lybækkerne, stadfæstede 1250 sin Halvsøster Fru Ingeborgs Gaver til Sorø Kloster, hvortil han selv s. A. gav Gods i Sørninge, ombyttede atter sit blekingske Hertugdømme med Laaland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Leo, Nachkommen Gorms des Alten, 1978 , Brenner, S. Otto, Reference: 193.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Leo, ~Europäische Stammtafeln, J.A. Stargardt Verlag, Marburg, Schwennicke, Detlev (Ed.), Reference: II 100; III 391b.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Danmarks Adels Aarbog, Thiset, Hiort-Lorenzen, Bobé, Teisen., (Dansk Adelsforening), [1884 - 2005]., DAA 1916:422.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hertug (Duke) Knut VALDEMARSEN Denmark, born Bef. 1221 in DENMARK; died October 15, 1260;
2 CONT
2 CONT married (1) Hedvig [Patronym unkn.] av Brandenburg; married (2) Hertuginne (Dutchess) Ingegerd [Patronym
2 CONT
2 CONT unkn.] av Pommeren.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Book:
2 CONT
2 CONT Forsandboka II.58.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hertug (Duke) Knut Valdemarsen Denmark 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canute,_Duke_of_Revalia
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute or Knud Valdemarsen (died 1260) was Duke of Revelia, Blekinge and Lolland, a bastard son of King Valdemar II of Denmark. Canute was the son of the king by his concubine, Helena Guttormsdotter, widow of an important Danish n
2 CONC obleman and daughter of the late Guttorm, Riksjarl of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father gave him lands in Estonia as a hereditary duchy in 1219. He was Duke of Reval 1219-23, but was dispossessed. As compensation, he was given Blekinge in 1242, which he held until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute supported the younger rebel brothers, Abel and Christopher, against King Eric IV of Denmark in 1247. The king forced him to exchange Blekinge temporarily for Lolland, but Blekinge was soon restored to Canute's possession.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute's wife was presumably a Wendic lady, from the ducal House of Pomerelia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He left two sons: Eric, Duke of Halland (died 1304) and Lord Svantepolk Knudsen (died ca. 1305).
2 CONT
2 CONT His land of Blekinge, with Lister, was given to his great-grandson lord Knut Folkason in the 1330s by King Magnus VII of Norway. Lord Knut's heirs continued to claim the lordship.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Valdemarsson av Danmark (död 1260), hertig av Reval (Tallinn). Utomäktenskaplig son till Valdemar II Sejr och Guttorm jarls dotter Helena.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
