1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Holmger Torkelsson (Båt)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Torkel Andersson and Kristina Ulfsdotter (Ama) 
2 CONT * The abutment of the perimeter wall's eastern range against this tower shows that the wall was added at a later date, along with (we now know) a northern tower. These additions were made no later than 1480, by which time Stensö w
2 CONC as a tenant farm. The earliest textual evidence for the farmstead is from 1369, when Stensö seems to have been the seat of Holmger Torkelsson of the Boat family and his wife Sigrid Karlsdotter of the Stubbe family, a recently marr
2 CONC ied couple in Sweden's top-level nobility (Dipl. Suec. 6108 & SDHK 7573). Lord Holmger's maternal grandfather Ulf Holmgersson was the son of Lady Kristina who owned Landsjö in c. 128
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ama#TAB_2 Ama Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT Holmger Ulfsson (d.), Also called Holmger Ama (son of Ulf Holmgersson, tab. 2). Is probably the "scolaris" Holmger, who along with his brother Lars 1288 is remembered in his "cognatus" archbishop Magnus Bosson's will. Incidentally
2 CONC , the earliest mentioned 1291. Became a knight by 1303. Was 1305 King Birger's camerarius. Died earlier in 1307 but before 1.2 1308 and buried in Alvastra monastery. Owned property in N. Vedbo and Tjusts hd in Småland and Boberg's
2 CONC  hd in Östergötland, in Hanekind's hd in the same landscape, in Villåttinge hd in Södermanland and at Västerås in Västmanland. Was married in 1307 to Ingegärd, who owned land in Västergötland and lived another 1308 and chose a bur
2 CONC ial ground in Alvastra monastery. - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ama#TAB_2
2 CONT
