2 CONT == Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters==
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Torkelsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=5&postid=sdhk_7574&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7574]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1359 July 30, of Issue: Stensö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Holmger Torkelsson''' announces that he and his brother the '''knight Magnus Torkelsson''' and several others' consent as a morning gift have given his wife '''Sigrid Karlsdotter''' 13 ½ öresland land in Norrlänna in Länna pari
2 CONC sh in Åkers district and 1 land land in Vävelsta in Husby-Oppunda parish and a mill in Djupvik with two villagers in (Ö.) Husby (now in Kvarsebo) parish in Östkinds district. If they have children, the morning gift should be count
2 CONC ed as the children's mothers. If Sigrid dies (childless) before Holmger, the morning present returns to him. If Holmger dies first, the morning present will be Sigrids. Advice has been obtained from Mr. Magnus Torkelsson and Haral
2 CONC d Ernilsson and Karl Tuveson. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/7574.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=SDHK+7573&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7573&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7573]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Dating: 1359 July 30, of Issue: Stensö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Holmger Torkelsson''' announces that he gave his '''wife Sigrid Karlsdotter''' a morning present on the right obstacle day according to the country's law. The "difference man" was the letter issuer's '''brother, the knight Magn
2 CONC us Torkelsson''' and the deputies the knights Magnus Nilsson (Röde) and Rörik (Tordsson) Bonde. Fasting were Sigrid's maternal uncle Mr Bengt Filipsson and Mr Ulf Håkansson, knights, and Johan Kristinason, Holmger Ama, Bengt Fader
2 CONC sson, Nils Ragnvaldsson, Birger Tureson, Magnus Nilsson, Johan Nilsson, Håkan Johansson, Inge Ingeson and Peter Guldsmed from Nyköping. The issuer seals. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/7573.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson+&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=9&postid=sdhk_7556&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7556]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1359 May 17, of Issue: Skanninge
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Holmger Torkelsson''' sells to the knight Magnus Nilsson all his estates in Västerlösa in Rogslösa parish (Dals district) for 200 marks Swedish money according to the country's law.
2 CONT The issuer and Mr. Magnus, Bengt Filipsson and '''Magnus Torkelsson,''' knights, and Mr. Harald, parish priest in Skänninge, Sjunne Klemensson, councilor in Skänninge, '''Harald Ernilsson''' and Karl Tuveson seal. - https://sok.ri
2 CONC ksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/7556.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=SDHK+4146&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_4146&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 4146]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1335 April 5'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Holmgersson, kanik in Uppsala and Västerås, bequeaths to the building of Uppsala Cathedral, where he chooses to be buried, a farm in Helgestad, and to the improvement of the prebenda he held in Västerås 6 öresland in Ulsa and 
2 CONC 1 öresland in Vikby. He decides on numerous gifts in the form of money and other things, among other things. a. Strängnäs Cathedral, Linköping Cathedral, Vårfruberga Monastery, '''Kristina Holmgersdotter,''' Alvastra Monastery, Ny
2 CONC dala Monastery, Varnhems Monastery, Julita Monastery, the Preacher Brothers in Strängnäs, Sigtuna, Västerås, Skara, Lödöse, Skänninge, Uppsala, Kalbr, Nöra Söderköping, Linköping, Jönköping, Skara, Arboga, Enköping, on to Sko klos
2 CONC ter, Askeby kloster, S: ta Klara kloster in Stockholm, helgeandshuset in Uppsala, spetälskehuset in Enköping, hospital in Strängnäs, Söderköping, Skänninge,
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus, '''Torkel Andersson,''' Birger Magnusson, and the issuer seal, SEAL
2 CONT The seal: N: o 1-5 away, the strips left; N: o 6, Ulf Holmgerssons (3 plugs). - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000049027095883&photo_id=6000000140042367915&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://aardvarchaeology.wordpress.com/2014/05/24/castle-owners/ Aardvarchaeology – by Dr. Martin Rundkvist]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Castle Owners'''
2 CONT
2 CONT My excavations this summer will target the ruins of two Medieval castles near Norrköping. Christian Lovén and I have selected these two because unusually, both have curtain walls (Sw. ringmur) but do not seem to have belonged to t
2 CONC he Crown. The High Middle Ages in Sweden are poorly documented in surviving written sources, but in one of these cases we actually have a pretty good idea who built the castle and when.
2 CONT
2 CONT Landsjö in Kimstad parish enters the record in about 1280 when an old woman writes her will. She’s Kristina, daughter of a certain Faste who had borne a plant device on his coat of arms and is otherwise forgotten, and she signs La
2 CONC ndsjö as her sätesgård manorial seat. Lady Kristina’s late husband, dead since about 1255, had been a well-known and powerful man: Lord Holmger, son of Folke jarl and male originator of the Ama family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The late 13th century saw the first major wave of masonry castle construction in Sweden, and so Landsjö castle is unlikely to pre-date 1250. On the other hand, after the Black Death in 1350 Landsjö was farmed by tenants and thus n
2 CONC o longer a manor of the nobility. Lady Kristina’s will marks a likely point in time when the castle would originally have been completed. In 1630 Landsjö again became a manor, a new säteri building was constructed elsewhere and th
2 CONC e old castle was heavily quarried for building materials. Since then little seems to have happened on the castle islet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Things are less clear at Stensö in Östra Husby. This castle starts as a single round kastal-type tower with no entrance from ground level, most likely about 1200. '''But the first written mention of the farmstead occurs only in 13
2 CONC 59, when it is the manor of Holmger Torkelsson of the Boat family.''' The castle has a curtain wall with some brick in it which is likely to have been added at some time during the preceding century. No later than 1480 this proper
2 CONC ty too loses its manorial status and is farmed by tenants.
2 CONT
2 CONT This 14th century Lord Holmger belonged to the high nobility. Both his father and his maternal grandfather were members of the Royal Council. The grandfather was Ulf Holmgersson of the Ama family, and wouldn’t you know it, the son
2 CONC  of Lady Kristina of Landsjö! Christian points out that the sources tell us Lord Ulf owned property near Stensö among other places, but we do not know where his seat was. A possible scenario is that the Ama family handed down both
2 CONC  ambitious castle-building traditions and the name Holmger from Lady Kristina’s time on. Today Stensö castle boasts one of Sweden’s best-preserved kastal towers, and it is particularly accessible since the 19th century when a land
2 CONC owner had most of the rubble cover carted away as lime-rich soil improvement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Neither of these sites have seen any documented excavations. I believe my team will be able to contribute a lot of interesting data in our four weeks of fieldwork.
2 CONT
