1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Who can verify this Anna and her existence or interconnection with Knud Jensen Barfod as his wife??? Even though she is in a place in Myheritage, it is in itself no verification.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name tags. In the past, it was the case that a large part of getting and subsequently wearing a name meant to be a relative. For example, they had children, to whom a father was father, the name of Hans in their surname. And until
2 CONC  about 1900, especially in the rural population, the oldest son was named after his grandfather, the oldest daughter after his grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Http://www.genealogi.dk/index.php/17-genealogi/for-dugar-igang/110-navnskikke Names in a family or family can provide good knowledge about the genus. What types of names did the children receive and were they named after older rel
2 CONC atives? As mentioned, every family has its history. Even though it is Hansen. In ancient times you got the name of the one you were the son or daughter of, the so-called "patronyns" or father names. Hans and Jens's sons and daught
2 CONC ers His father Hans came to his sons Hansen, the daughters Hansdatter. It is only about 150 years ago, that system ceased to be called Hansen, Jensen or Pedersen, is it nice to know who it was Hans, Jens or Peder, whose name is na
2 CONC med after. And similarly, if you have a more rare name, you must try to track its origins, whether Danish or foreign. Actually, the patronyms ceased with the name act of May 30, 1828, which prompted genealogies, but in the broad-b
2 CONC ased population, a celebration of the old nameship was held for many decades. It was common sense, for example, to call a boy to Jens Pedersen, if his father was called Hans Pedersen. Then it seemed that they were more siblings th
2 CONC an father and son. The knight should be called what he was, namely Jens Hans-son. Only very slowly and after an indentation in 1856, the new naming methods were developed. Call waiting First names were usually given by call, so th
2 CONC e oldest son got grandfather's name, oldest girl got grandmother and then went to grandparents. But there could of course be many variations if the grandparents had died and their grandparents lived, they would often call the dead
2 CONC  before they were alive. Had a husband or wife been married before, the first child in the new marriage should preferably bear the name of the deceased spouse, deceased siblings should be called, which could be particularly nice o
2 CONC r profitable in the mothers that you would like to call and therefore broke or Bend the conventions a little.
