1 NAME Peder Jensson /Rui/
2 GIVN Peder Jensson
2 SURN Rui
2 _MARNM Skanderup
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1683
2 ADDR
3 STAE Telemark
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1765
2 PLAC Tudal
2 ADDR
3 STAE Telemark
1 BURI
2 DATE 3 MAR 1765
2 PLAC Siljan Lutheran Cemetery, Siljan, Telemark, Norway
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Peder Jensen was born in Tudal, Siljan, Telemark, Norway, in 1683. He died in Tudal, Siljan, Telemark, Norway, in 1765 at the age of 82. Peder was buried in Siljan Cemetery, Siljan, Telemark, Norway, on March 03, 1765. He married 
2 CONC Marte Svendsdatter.
2 CONT Peder and Marte lived for a time in Seljord and baptized children living at Eiulvsås in 1712 and 1715. They then baptized children living at Tveiten in Seljord from 1718 to 1724. They probably also had a child around 1726, their s
2 CONC on Jens. He may also have been born in Seljord. Then they have another son, Zacharias. Based on his age, when he died, he was born before they married, but here there is a good chance that the age may be incorrectly stated when he
2 CONC  died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder and his family came to Mustvedt in Gjerpen where he is mentioned as a tenant. (He is mentioned there about 1727 according to gamlegjerpen.no ) His mother, Magdalene Schanke , did not die in Seljord, but came to (or with) her
2 CONC  son at / to Mustvedt in Gjerpen and died there in 1741. She was buried 08.03.1741 as "Per Mustveds mother Malene, 85 years".
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder had a brother Jacob Jensen who married Gunhild Jørgensdatter and who lived at Kosi in Seljord. We find him as the sponsor of Peder's children. A son of this Jacob Jensen, Zacharias Jacobsen, came to Kleven in Gjerpen. See ga
2 CONC mlergjerpen.no
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Jensen was born in Tudal, Siljan, Telemark, Norway, in 1683. He died in Tudal, Siljan, Telemark, Norway, in 1765 at the age of 82. Peder was buried in Siljan Cemetery, Siljan, Telemark, Norway, on March 03, 1765. He married 
2 CONC Marte Svendsdatter.
2 CONT Peder and Marte lived for a time in Seljord and baptized children living at Eiulvsås in 1712 and 1715. They then baptized children living at Tveiten in Seljord from 1718 to 1724. They probably also had a child around 1726, their s
